\begin{enumerate}
    \item $K + L = 340$
    \item $L = 4K + 10$
\end{enumerate}
We can substitute the second equation into the first equation to solve for $K$:
$K + (4K + 10) = 340$
$5K + 10 = 340$
$5K = 340 - 10$
$5K = 330$
$K = \frac{330}{5}$
$K = 66$
Now we can substitute $K = 66$ into the second equation to find $L$:
$L = 4(66) + 10$
$L = 264 + 10$
$L = 274$
So Kylie picked 66 apples and Kayla picked 274 apples.
The number of apples Kayla picked is 274.
